course: dictionary
lesson: 4036
title: One little word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ge is a tricky little word. On its own it is not an English word. It is a piece of longer words, like «age», «gem» and «get», so you have to look at the whole word to know what it means.
explain: In Mandarin Chinese, ge is a measure word. «ge is the everyday all-rounder», so you put it between a number and a noun, as in «yí ge» (one of). A measure word paints a little picture of the shape: long bendy things take tiáo, flat things take zhāng, and books take běn.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Read the words around ge, then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense. Ge can also be a chemistry symbol or an abbreviation, so always check where you found it.
fact: Ge on its own is not an English word; it is a piece of longer words like «age», «gem» and «get».
fact: The chemical symbol Ge stands for germanium, a grey element used in electronics.
fact: GE can stand for General Electric, an American company, or for «general election» in news talk.
fact: In Greek myths, Ge (also Gaia) is the goddess of the Earth.
fact: In Mandarin, ge is the everyday measure word: «yí ge» means one of something, and «liǎng ge rén» means two people.
exercise: Is ge a word you can use alone in an English sentence? | Yes, it means very big | Yes, it is a Greek goddess | *No, it is only a piece of longer words like age, gem and get | No, it is a number
exercise: «ge is the everyday all-rounder, but long bendy things take tiáo, and books take běn.» Which measure word is the everyday all-rounder? | tiáo | běn | zhāng | *ge
exercise: In news talk, what can GE stand for? | Gold Earth | Good Eating | Greek Empire | *General election
test: Which element has the chemical symbol Ge? | Silver | *Germanium | Gold | Neon
test: In Greek myths, who is Ge? | A river god | A talking bird | A king of the sea | *The goddess of the Earth
exam: Which is the best way to check a meaning from context? | Stop reading at once | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Ignore the sentence and guess | Pick the longest word
